; Host - which target this compiler binary itself runs on.
; See `Host.darwin-aarch64.ax` for why this is a compile-time constant
; selected by module resolution rather than a runtime query.
;
; No compiler runs on this target - it answers only so that a build
; FOR the part resolves the module at all. None of the port's values
; live here: `docs/embedded-proposal.md` 4.1 records why a
; cross-compiling host must not answer the target's constants.
(pub :: hostTarget String)
(pub fn (hostTarget)
  "baremetal-aarch64")
